Package: cgrc.bayes
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Implementation of the Correct Guess Rate Curve
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Dave", "Smith", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "fish.dzs0017@gmail.com")
Description: Reproduces the Correct Guess Rate Curve (CGRC) of Szigeti et al.
    (2023) <doi:10.1038/s41598-023-34938-7>, which adjusts a trial's treatment
    contrast for unblinding by reweighting participants to a target
    correct-guess rate, and reports the uncertainty around the adjusted
    contrast as a posterior distribution instead of through resampling. The
    estimand is unchanged. Provides a conjugate Normal-Inverse-Gamma posterior,
    a matching JAGS backend with an agreement check, the original kernel
    density resampling procedure for comparison, the activated-expectancy-bias
    simulation model for checking a design before analysis, a region of
    practical equivalence decomposition, and an interactive Shiny app. Also
    implements a proposed extension, not part of the original method, that
    keeps "I don't know" guesses as a third response category.
